{
  "_comment": [
    "Class progressions, for the arithmetic the sheet does on a player's behalf.",
    "",
    "This file holds only what is mechanical and fixed: the hit die, the three",
    "progressions, the skill points, and the class skill list. Class FEATURES",
    "(rage, sneak attack, spells per day) are not here. They are the interesting",
    "half of a class and the half this campaign alters most, so they stay on the",
    "wiki where they can be read, and the sheet keeps them as free text.",
    "",
    "  bab    good = +1/level, average = +3/4 level, poor = +1/2 level",
    "  saves  good = 2 + level/2, poor = level/3, both rounded down",
    "  srd    true when the numbers come from the SRD and need no checking",
    "",
    "A class not listed here is not a problem: a player adds it once, by hand,",
    "under Custom Classes, and it then behaves exactly like one of these.",
    "Splatbook and prestige classes are expected to arrive that way.",
    "",
    "  casting / manifesting  the ability a caster or manifester uses, and:",
    "    spontaneous  casts without preparing (bard, sorcerer)",
    "    spellbook    prepares from a spellbook of spells learned (wizard)",
    "    half         caster level is half the class level (paladin, ranger)",
    "    domains      chooses two domains, each with a slot a level (cleric)",
    "    disciplines  chooses a discipline, with its own powers (psion)",
    "  Spells per day, spells known and power points come from data/srd/progression.json.",
    "",
    "  startingGold   the SRD's random starting gold, and its average - a 1st-level character's wealth",
    "  bonusFeats     class bonus feats: at `levels`, from a named `list` (fighter, wizard, psion,",
    "                 psychicWarrior); or `choices` of named feats by level, which a monk or a",
    "                 ranger takes without the prerequisites",
    "  grantedFeats   feats the class simply gives, which take no slot",
    "  languages      bonus languages the class adds to its race's, and any it knows automatically"
  ],
